Z||000001||Bob Englert||12-05-2000||09:13 PM||||If it is an 85 GT it will be a 4 sp transmission.  6 cyl Fieros didn't come with a 5 sp until the end of the 86 model year when the Getrag was added in place of the 4 sp.<P>It is possible that someone replaced the 4 sp with a 5 sp, but that would invite a whole host of additional questions....<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||kinboyatuwo||12-05-2000||09:16 PM||||like what, <BR>how hard is the swap and is it worth it <BR>hey why not have lots of questions answered at once<BR>less posts<BR>right!||||reg||1
Z||000003||Bob Englert||12-05-2000||11:20 PM||||If I was looking at a car that had a different transmission from what came with it when new I would be very careful.  When buying a car with an engine or transmission transplant calls to mind the qaulity of the conversion.  <P>For every engine or transmission convrsion that I See at a show that is done really well there is probably 3 that are 1/2 done or patched together enough for the owner to unload it on someone else.  I would be very careful about someone else's cusomizing work.<P>In any case, you will know which transmission you have as soon as you try to put it in reverse!<BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
